  "proof_and_test": [
    "Every overlay write inserts a tops entry, even an air/mask-zero write; snapshots and before-feature rollback preserve that membership with the writes. Without a column entry, Field.height already describes the live state. Field prior, substrate and fallback paths return the predicate height.",
    "Existing deferred-ore proof requires all six required/output heightmap bits to match. Height-only lookup can skip a consecutive suffix of such roots. Material lookup retains its exact original prefix, and an earlier state is never cached as the current material view.",
    "The new test checks all six untouched heights without material reads, rollback to the untouched view, clearing the top block, adding and then clearing a higher block with stale top metadata, and an untouched neighboring column."
  ],
